# Next.js 16

Check unfamiliar APIs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (the Next.js block in `AGENTS.md` points there too).

## Rendering

- `src/app` files are Server Components. `"use client"` only on leaf components that need state, effects, events or browser APIs, never on `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx`.
- `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()` and `headers()` are async: `const { id } = await params`.
- Stream with `loading.tsx` and `<Suspense>`; add `error.tsx` and `not-found.tsx` where a segment can fail or miss.
- Metadata via `metadata` or `generateMetadata`, never manual `<head>` tags.
- `next/dynamic` with `{ ssr: false }` works only inside Client Components.

## Data and caching

- Prefetch with `queryClient.prefetchQuery(options)` on the server and hand off with `HydrationBoundary`; clients read it with the feature's query hook.
- `"use cache"` (`cacheLife`, `cacheTag`) only with `cacheComponents: true` in `next.config.ts`. Read cookies and headers outside cached scopes.
- Pass only serializable, non-sensitive data to Client Components. Import `server-only` in server-only modules.

## Server Actions

- One file per action in `features/<feature>/actions/`, `"use server"` at the top. Never inline.
- Validate with the feature's Zod schema, check auth, then call the api layer (no direct database access). Return `{ data, error }`, never raw errors.

## proxy.ts

- `src/proxy.ts` replaces `middleware.ts`. Only redirects, rewrites, headers and locale; no data fetching.

## Assets

- `next/image`, `next/font` and `next/script`. LCP image: `loading="eager"` or `fetchPriority="high"` (`preload` replaces the deprecated `priority`).
<!-- i18n:start -->

## i18n

- `next-intl`: routes live under `src/app/[locale]`, config in `src/i18n/`. See the `i18n` rule.
<!-- i18n:end -->

<example>
```tsx
// src/app/users/[id]/page.tsx
import { dehydrate, HydrationBoundary } from "@tanstack/react-query";

import { makeQueryClient } from "@/lib/query-client";

import { UserProfile, userQueryOptions } from "@/features/users";

type PageProps = { params: Promise<{ id: string }> };

export default async function UserPage({ params }: PageProps) {
  const { id } = await params;
  const queryClient = makeQueryClient();
  await queryClient.prefetchQuery(userQueryOptions(id));

  return (
    <HydrationBoundary state={dehydrate(queryClient)}>
      <UserProfile id={id} />
    </HydrationBoundary>
  );
}
```
</example>

<incorrect-example>
```tsx
"use client";
export default function Page() {
  useEffect(() => { fetch("/api/user").then(setUser); }, []);
}
```
</incorrect-example>
